---@meta
-- Generated by rs3-api-types from https://developer.runescape.com/rs/game/config/npctype.html;
-- regenerate it with ./gradlew generate rather than editing it.

---An `NPCType` config contains the descriptive data necessary for the game to construct an NPCEntity.
---
---These config types can be found within the `config.NPC` table:
---
---Info: An `NPCType` is a Proxy usertype, which means it is safe to copy and store in your scripts. It cannot, however,
---be used with any persistent storage.
---
---Information available within an `NPCType` includes:
---
---MultiNPC: MultiNPCs are special `NPCType` configs which allow an NPCEntity to select one of many child `NPCTypes`
---based on a variable value.
---
---For example, an NPCEntity could swap between several `NPCTypes`, with different appearances and/or minimenu options,
---based on a variable value. It could also be made invisible, if no `NPCType` is assigned to the current variable
---value.
---@class NPCType
---@field id integer (Read-only) The ID of this config type.
---@field configName string (Read-only) The name of this config, i.e. `"HANS"`.
---@field typeName string (Read-only) The type of this config. Will always be `"NPC"`.
---@field name string (Read-only) The display name of this config type.
---@field attackOpHasPriority boolean (Read-only) Whether the `Attack` op of an NPCEntity using this config is given priority. Used in combination with `Player.GetAttackOpPriority`.
---@field visibleCombatLevel integer (Read-only) The combat level presented for an entity using this config.
---@field castsShadows boolean (Read-only) Whether an NPCEntity using this config should cast a shadow.
---@field overlayHeight integer (Read-only) A custom override for how far above an NPCEntity to draw its overlays. Value is `-1` if unused.
---@field walkSmoothing boolean (Read-only) Whether an NPCEntity using this config should follow walk routes smoothly. A smooth route uses bezier curves and acceleration. A non-smooth route travels linearly through tile centres.
---@field isExamineOnly boolean (Read-only) Shorthand check for whether this config type contains only an `Examine` op.
---@field attackOpIndex integer (Read-only) The op index for this configs `Attack` op. Returns `-1` if none is set.
---@field examineOpIndex integer (Read-only) The op index for this configs `Examine` op. Returns `-1` if none is set.
---@field firstUniqueOpIndex integer (Read-only) The op index where the first non-standard op begins. Returns `-1` if none is set.
---@field opNames table<integer, string> (Read-only) A list of names shown for the available ops in this config. Use `pairs()` to iterate this list, which will provide both the op index and name as `opIndex,opName`.
---@field bas BaseAnimSetType? (Read-only) The animation set used by this config. Returns `nil` if none is set.
---@field fastPicking boolean (Read-only) Whether an NPCEntity using this config uses a lower accuracy, but faster, picking test on triangles.
---@field roughBounding integer (Read-only) Whether an NPCEntity using this config should skip triangle tests and stop at an earlier rectangular bounds test. `-1` = Only if `gridSize == 1` `0` = Never `1` = Always
---@field resize Vector3 (Read-only) A scaling transform applied to the body model(s) of an NPCEntity using this config.
---@field gridSize integer (Read-only) The reported tile size of an NPCEntity using this config. Used in various entity logic and priority checks.
---@field turnSpeed integer (Read-only) The turning speed of an NPCEntity using this config. Affects facing and movement turn speeds.
---@field wanderRange integer (Read-only) The maximum tile distance an NPCEntity will wander from its current coordinate when starting a new wander move.
---@field maxRange integer (Read-only) The maximum tile distance an NPCEntity can move from its spawning coordinate. Also the maximum tile distance from its spawning coordinate at which it will pay attention to a PlayerEntity.
---@field isActive boolean (Read-only) Whether an NPCEntity using this config is considered active. An inactive entity is not shown on the minimap and will not show in the minimenu.
---@field isFamiliar boolean (Read-only) Whether an NPCEntity using this config is considered a familiar. Familiar-type NPCs have a lower draw order priority.
---@field isAlwaysOnTop boolean (Read-only) Greatly advances the draw order priority of an NPCEntity using this config. Not guaranteed to be on top.
---@field isAlwaysOnBottom boolean (Read-only) Reduces the draw order priority of an NPCEntity using this config. Not guaranteed to be at bottom.
---@field priorityOffset integer (Read-only) Adjusts the draw order priority of an NPCEntity using this config. Can be positive or negative.
---@field isOnMiniMap boolean (Read-only) Whether an NPCEntity using this config is shown on the minimap.
---@field mapElement MapElementType? (Read-only) The map element to display for this config. Returns `nil` if none is set.
---@field quests QuestTypeConfig[] (Read-only) A list of all quests related to this config.
---@field isMultiNPC boolean (Read-only) Whether this config contains a sub-list of `NPCTypes` and a `multiVar` variable to use in selecting one. An NPCEntity which uses a multiNPC config will expose it through NPCEntity.parentConfig, while the selected `NPCType` sub-list config is exposed through NPCEntity.config.
---@field multiVar VarType? (Read-only) The variable which controls the currently displayed `NPCType`.
---@field hasCustomBounding boolean (Read-only) Whether an NPCEntity using this config uses an overriding AABB bounds for picking tests. Often used by NPCs which have geometry or animations that make them tricky to click.
---@field customBounding AABB? (Read-only) The AABB which describes this configs custom bounds. Returns `nil` if none is set.
---@field hasBackgroundSound boolean (Read-only) Whether an NPCEntity using this config should play a sound depending on its animation state. Indicates that at least one of the ready/crawl/walk/run sounds is set.
---@field backgroundSoundReady integer (Read-only) TODO: Will become a config type
---@field backgroundSoundCrawl integer (Read-only) TODO: Will become a config type
---@field backgroundSoundWalk integer (Read-only) TODO: Will become a config type
---@field backgroundSoundRun integer (Read-only) TODO: Will become a config type
---@field backgroundSoundRange integer (Read-only) The maximum tile range, in `Grid units`, of any background sounds played by an NPCEntity using this config. Distances above this range set volume to 0%.
---@field backgroundSoundDropoffRange integer (Read-only) The tile distance, in `Grid units`, at which background sounds in this config begin to drop off in volume. Distances below this range set volume to 100%.
---@field backgroundSoundVolume integer (Read-only) The base volume of any background sounds played by an NPCEntity using this config.
---@field params ParamType[] (Read-only) Returns a list of all the ParamTypes stored in this config.
---@field paramCount integer (Read-only) How many params this config has.
local NPCType = {}

---Returns the custom CursorType, if any, used for the given op index.
---@param opIndex integer The op index. Valid values are `1` -> `6`
---@return CursorType? # The cursor type to display. Returns `nil` if no op exists for this index, or no custom CursorType is set on an existing op.
function NPCType:GetOpCursor(opIndex) end

---Returns the corresponding output value for the given input ParamType.
---@param param ParamType The input param value.
---@return any # The corresponding output value. Returns `param.defaultValue` if the param is not found in the data structure.
function NPCType:GetParamValue(param) end

---Returns whether this config contains output data for the given input ParamType.
---@param param ParamType The input param value.
---@return boolean # Whether a corresponding value exists in this config for ParamType.
function NPCType:HasParam(param) end
